Z||000000||Johnson's85SE||12-13-2000||04:43 PM||||I read Fierosounds approach to dual boxes behind the seats. I stripped everything down, to the firewall. drilled my first hole, and was about to cut out a square in the firewall when i saw light threw the hole to the ground. I lost my nerve, and just decided to not cut. The firewall is not a flat angle to the floor. So many annoying angles would need to be cut. So with snow on the ground, We just put a layer of MDF over the back of the boxes. Intotal we lost about 3-4 inchs by not using the firewall as the back of the box, and not cutting a hole in the firewall for the magnet. When summer comes, I will cut a hole, cause I need the space back. Constant crying from passangers. I love the sound though, put in two 10' Ultimate SB10's. need only an air space of .75 to 1.0 sealed. 125 Watts RMS. Not huge power subs. Running with a Alpine V12 250. <BR>Cheers!<P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||3
